 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? It' usually the groom's side covering the hotel, the flowers, the venue, and some of the food. The bride's family often helps with the outfits and travel costs. That' a fair starting point. His parents might still chip in, or offer to cover more if you' unsure. Not rude at all, it' a common question, and it's better to ask now than on the day. Then ask your parents directly. Most parents are happy to help, especially if you offer to chip in too. Good idea. Just make sure you both agree on the final number.",
